Wildcard Aliases provides firewall aliases for wildcard domain patterns such as
*.core.windows.net, which cannot be resolved ahead of time.

A small DNS forwarder sits in the resolver chain (for example as a per-domain
upstream of Unbound or AdGuard Home). For every answer to a matching name it
adds the returned addresses to a pf table before the answer is passed on to
the client, and removes them again once the DNS TTL (plus a grace period) has
expired. Each table is available as an "External (advanced)" alias for use in
regular firewall rules.

